@page "/custom-profiles"

<PageTitle>Custom profiles</PageTitle>
<h1>Custom profiles</h1>
<p><code>ProfiledValidator&lt;T&gt;</code> composes arbitrary named rulesets, not just the built-in draft/submit pair. This page picks a profile at runtime. The engine reads <code>Options</code> only when it binds a new <code>Model</code>, so the picker resets the form with a fresh model instance alongside the new options to make the change take effect.</p>

<TeachingPanel CodeFiles="@(new[] { "ReviewedPost.cs", "CustomProfiles.razor", "CustomProfiles.razor.cs" })">
    <Rules>
        <ul>
            <li>Profiles are just named rule-set selections. <code>Draft</code> and <code>Submit</code> are the two built-ins <code>DraftSubmitValidator</code> wires up for you; this page's validator defines a third, <strong>AdminReview</strong>, which also includes <code>Submit</code>'s rules.</li>
            <li><strong>Title</strong>: required under every profile (a common rule).</li>
            <li><strong>Slug</strong>: required under the <code>Submit</code> ruleset.</li>
            <li><strong>Category</strong>: required under <code>Submit</code>. A <code>FormidableInputSelect</code> with <code>UpdateOn="OnBlur"</code>: picking an option commits it at once, but the message waits until you leave the control.</li>
            <li><strong>Read minutes</strong>: a whole number from 1 to 180 under <code>Submit</code>. A <code>FormidableInputNumber</code>: an entry the box cannot parse (try <code>e3</code>) never reaches the model, never raises a message of its own, and clears from the box when you tab away, so FluentValidation's required and range messages stay the only word on the field.</li>
            <li><strong>Publish date</strong>: required under <code>Submit</code>. A <code>FormidableInputDate</code> with <code>UpdateOn="OnBlur"</code>, the recommended pairing for a date input.</li>
            <li><strong>Review note</strong>: required only under the <code>AdminReview</code> ruleset.</li>
            <li>The picker rebuilds the form on change: <code>FormidableForm</code> only reads its <code>Options</code> parameter when the <code>Model</code> reference changes, so a profile swap needs a fresh model instance to take effect.</li>
        </ul>
    </Rules>
    <TryIt>
        <ol>
            <li>With <em>Standard submit</em> selected, submit with everything empty — Category shows "Category is required" among the rest. Pick a category — the message waits until you leave the control, so it still reads "required" right after you pick; tab away and it clears.</li>
            <li>Fill Title, Slug, Read minutes and Publish date, leave Review note empty, and submit — it goes through.</li>
            <li>Switch to <em>Admin review</em> — the form resets. Enter the same fields and submit — blocked: the review note is now required.</li>
            <li>Fill in Review note and submit again — it goes through under admin review.</li>
        </ol>
    </TryIt>
</TeachingPanel>

<fieldset>
    <legend>Profile</legend>
    <label><input type="radio" name="profile" checked="@(!_adminReview)" @onchange="() => SelectProfile(false)" /> Standard submit</label>
    <label><input type="radio" name="profile" checked="@_adminReview" @onchange="() => SelectProfile(true)" /> Admin review</label>
</fieldset>

<FormidableForm @ref="_form" Model="_post" Options="_options">
    <div class="summary-slot">
        <FormidableSummary />
    </div>

    <div class="field"><label>Title <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_post.Title" /></label>
        <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _post.Title" /></div>
    <div class="field"><label>Slug <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_post.Slug" /></label>
        <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _post.Slug" /></div>
    <div class="field">
        <label for="@CategoryId">Category</label>
        <FormidableInputSelect @bind-Value="_post.Category" UpdateOn="InputUpdateMode.OnBlur">
            <option value="">Choose…</option>
            <option>Announcement</option>
            <option>Tutorial</option>
            <option>Release notes</option>
        </FormidableInputSelect>
        <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _post.Category" />
    </div>
    <div class="field"><label>Read minutes <FormidableInputNumber @bind-Value="_post.ReadMinutes" /></label>
        <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _post.ReadMinutes" /></div>
    <div class="field"><label>Publish date <FormidableInputDate @bind-Value="_post.PublishDate" UpdateOn="InputUpdateMode.OnBlur" /></label>
        <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _post.PublishDate" /></div>
    <div class="field"><label>Review note <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_post.ReviewNote" /></label>
        <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _post.ReviewNote" /></div>

    <div class="actions"><button type="button" class="primary" @onclick="Submit">Submit</button></div>
</FormidableForm>

<p role="status">@_status</p>
